{"name":"Sago","hex":"#d8cfc3","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Sago","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Sago"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sago","blocks":[{"text":"Sago is a starch extracted from the soft, spongy core tissue of several tropical palm species, especially Metroxylon sagu. For centuries, it has been an important traditional staple food among many indigenous communities across the islands of Southeast Asia and the Melanesian region, including Malaysia, Indonesia, and Papua New Guinea. In different regions, sago is also known by local names such as saksak, rabia, and sagu."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Sago_%28Metroxylon_sagu%29_in_New_Guinea.jpg/330px-Sago_%28Metroxylon_sagu%29_in_New_Guinea.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sago","wikidata":"Q218778"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Metroxylon_sagu%2C_Sago_Preparation.jpg/500px-Metroxylon_sagu%2C_Sago_Preparation.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Metroxylon_sagu%2C_Sago_Preparation.jpg/500px-Metroxylon_sagu%2C_Sago_Preparation.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Peeling and pounding a segment of sago palm stem to produce an edible starch. Sepik River, Papua New Guinea","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMetroxylon_sagu%2C_Sago_Preparation.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Sago_Palm_being_harvested_for_Sago_production_PNG.jpg/500px-Sago_Palm_being_harvested_for_Sago_production_PNG.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Sago_Palm_being_harvested_for